{"name":"Polar Ice","hex":"#71a6d2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"polar ice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Permanent sea ice found in the Arctic and Antarctic"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polar_ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Polar Ice (vodka)","blocks":[{"text":"Polar Ice is a Canadian vodka produced by Corby Distilleries Ltd. Produced from Canadian corn, it is quadruple-distilled, which vendors claim rids it of microscopic impurities and gives it a smoother taste. It is an 80 proof spirit. The product line includes various sizes and bottles of Polar Ice Vodka, Polar Ice Vodka Arctic Extreme and Polar Ice Vodka Ontario Peach. It is sold across Canada and in some cities in the United States of America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Polar_Ice_Vodka_Bottle.jpg/330px-Polar_Ice_Vodka_Bottle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_Ice_(vodka)","wikidata":"Q7209033"},{"title":"Polar ice cap","blocks":[{"text":"A polar ice cap or polar cap is a high-latitude region of a planet, dwarf planet, or natural satellite that is covered in ice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Mars%2C_as_seen_by_the_Hubble_Telescope.jpg/330px-Mars%2C_as_seen_by_the_Hubble_Telescope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_ice_cap","wikidata":"Q1286914"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/North_pole_september_ice-pack_1978-2002.png/120px-North_pole_september_ice-pack_1978-2002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/North_pole_september_ice-pack_1978-2002.png/250px-North_pole_september_ice-pack_1978-2002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/North_pole_september_ice-pack_1978-2002.png/120px-North_pole_september_ice-pack_1978-2002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorth_pole_september_ice-pack_1978-2002.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/North_pole_february_ice-pack_1978-2002.png/120px-North_pole_february_ice-pack_1978-2002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/North_pole_february_ice-pack_1978-2002.png/250px-North_pole_february_ice-pack_1978-2002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/North_pole_february_ice-pack_1978-2002.png/120px-North_pole_february_ice-pack_1978-2002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorth_pole_february_ice-pack_1978-2002.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/